<p>(2) Numbers expressed are at end of period. NOTE: For the quarter ended December 31, 1996, earnings before an extraordinary item were $5.5 million, or $0.27 per share, an increase of 40.0% over the earnings before merger-related expenses of $3.9 million, or $0.19 per share, reported for the quarter ended December 31, 1995.  Costs associated with the January 1997 closure of an outpatient surgery center acquired as part of the December 1995 acquisition of Helian Health Group, Inc. were reported as an extraordinary item of $1.1 million, net of tax, or $0.06 per share, during the quarter ended December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>Earnings before the extraordinary item were $22.7 million, or $1.11 per share, for the year ended December 31, 1996, an increase of 46.2% over 1995 earnings before non-recurring charges for merger-related expenses and early debt extinguishment of $15.5 million, or $0.76 per share.  After non-recurring charges, the Company reported net income of $21.6 million, or $1.05 per share, for the year ended December 31, 1996, up 99.3% over the $10.8 million, or $0.53 per share, for 1995.</p>
